  "body": "Stacked on #4380 (merge #4380 first). This branch starts from the #4380 head `31438caa1`. Until #4380 merges, the diff against `main` also shows the #4380 changes. My own change is the last commit, `9351f22ec`.\n\n#4380 now has two more commits (`15626f333`, `2acc52c3e`, to `2acc52c3e`). They change only post and UI drilling files, and no file of this PR. This branch does not include them yet. It takes `main` after #4380 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe playback code moves from `camcraft-app` to `camcraft-sim`. Only the world reads stay in app.\n\n- These files move to `crates/sim/src/` with `git mv`:\n  - `stock_play.rs` to `play.rs` (`FieldPlay`).\n  - `stock_play_index.rs` to `play_index.rs` (`PlayIndex`, and the new plain inputs `PlayInputs` and `PlayOpPlan`).\n  - `stock_play_head.rs` to `play_head.rs`, and `stock_play_cut.rs` to `play_cut.rs`.\n  - `stock_play_precalc.rs` to `play_bind.rs`. The name `play_precalc` is already in use in sim.\n  - `stock_play_worker.rs`, `stock_play_worker_frame.rs` and `stock_play_worker_precalc.rs` to `play_worker*.rs`.\n- The plain-data parts that `FieldPlay` reads also move to sim:\n  - `FieldView`, `Packed`, `CutLayer`, `PackedBase`, `DEFAULT_TEXELS`, `build_stock`, `build_target` and `subdivide` go to `camcraft_sim::field_view`.\n  - `rotary_pose_tol` and `simulate_rotary_slice` go to `camcraft_sim::stock_sim` (`rotary_slice.rs`).\n  - `LathePlan` goes to `camcraft_sim::stock_sim` (`lathe_plan.rs`).\n- App re-exports each moved item at its old path. The paths are `stock_play`, `stock_play_worker`, `stock_view`, `stock_sim::rotary` and `stock_sim::lathe`.\n- `PlaySeed` is now an app newtype over `PlayInputs`. `PlaySeed::gather` reads the world. It also converts each `Planned` op to a `PlayOpPlan`.\n- `FieldPlay::from_seed` and the `PlayWorker::spawn*` functions take `impl Into<PlayInputs>`. Callers that pass a `PlaySeed` do not change.\n- `FieldPlay::new` and `FieldPlay::with_budget` read the world. They are now the methods of the app trait `stock_play::FieldPlayWorld`. Three test files import that trait. No assertion changed.\n- The worker reads the host clock from `PlayInputs::clock`. App passes `clock::monotonic`, which uses the #31 wasm32 clock seam. camcraft-sim gets no new dependency.\n- The Gate maps of the playback suites name the new sim modules. Then a change in `crates/sim/src/play*.rs` selects them in the quick gate.\n\nThe picture, the Deviate verdict and the post gate do not change. The cut code is the same code. Only its imports, the seed conversion and the clock reads changed.\n\n## Cause\n\nAGENTS.md \"app holds the document, nothing else\". The review of PR #2192 found that `FieldPlay` and `PlayWorker` hold domain logic in app.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins (new unit tests in the `camcraft-sim` lib, `crates/sim/src/play_tests.rs`, no new test binary). They build and drive the playback from plain inputs, with no world:\n  - `play::tests::field_play_cuts_plain_inputs_with_no_world`\n  - `play::tests::play_worker_lands_on_the_end_from_plain_inputs`\n  - `play::tests::play_index_maps_a_playhead_by_name`\n- Red before the change: yes. On the unchanged code the pins do not compile: `error[E0432]: unresolved imports super::FieldPlay, super::PlayInputs, super::PlayOpPlan, super::Progress` and `unresolved import crate::play_worker`.\n- Mutation: I put back the base `crates/sim/src/lib.rs` (no `play`, `play_worker` and `field_view` modules). The pins went red with the same E0432 errors. I restored the file, and the pins went green (3 passed).\n- The playback suites pass with no assertion change: `stock_play`, `stock_play_partial`, `stock_play_precalc`, `stock_play_picture`, `stock_play_stop`, `stock_play_cost_bench`, `stock_view`, `sim_op_step_stock`, `fidelity_copies`.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`) on the tree of `9351f22ec` before the decision file was added: 441 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 78.4 min. The steps include the #4380 diff. My diff alone (`--base` #4380 head) selects 96 of those steps.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-ui --tests`: clean. The UI source did not change.\n- Example catalog suites: not run. This PR changes no toolpath and no post.\n- Light lane: not run. Its six twins are toolpath generator tests (motion adaptive, app pocket start). This PR changes no generator.\n- Heavy lanes: not run. This is a P7 refactor. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" gives a heavy step only to a P1 PR under the safety floor.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. This PR's own commit changes no `.nc`, `.cl` or catalog file.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A wasm32 build. The clock seam is the same `clock::Instant` as before.\n- The GPU layer mode on a real GPU (`play_layer_gpu`). The UI code did not change, and it compiles.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4380 moves `PlayIndex` and `PlaySeed` to `stock_play_index.rs`. This PR moves that file to sim, so it is stacked on #4380.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/2268-play-to-sim.md`.\n\nChangelog: none (internal refactor: the playback moves from camcraft-app to camcraft-sim; no behaviour change).\n\nEffort: high\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2268#issuecomment-7229147903\n\nFixes #2268\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
